{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_newparts_parts_v_to_viii", "label": "New Parts V\u2013VIII (Past/Present/Future, What Cannot Be Removed, The One Coupling, Two Indices)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_balance_defect_1268", "label": "The Balance and Its 1,268 Defect", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "\u00a712.6.1 presents the q-factorisation as though the transfer were doing the work; the computation says the tree is doing it, since all four cuts \u2113, q, f, g give defect zero and q is distinguished only by which two things it separates."}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_pushback", "label": "Pushback \u2014 No Cell Can Be Removed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "J(x) and M(x) recomputed from x's own down-set and up-set agree with the global count on 930/930 and 934/934 cells, so pushback is a property of the interval and of nothing outside it. J(x) = 0 exactly on the join-irreducibles and M(x) = 0 exactly on the meet-irreducibles, 17 each \u2014 Birkhoff's count reproduced by an unrelated route. The distribution is U-shaped in rank: an index's resistance to deletion is weakest where it is widest."}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_step_law", "label": "The Step Law (prime, not irreducible)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The first statement used 'irreducible' and disagreed with the truth on 35 of 116,138 intervals \u2014 exactly 17 + 17 + 1. Convention excludes \u22a5 from the join-irreducibles, but the property the proof uses is primeness, which \u22a5 satisfies trivially; with 'prime' there are 0 disagreements, exhaustively."}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_cut_law", "label": "The Cut Law", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "89 component tests across all seven tower stages and every cut, one violation \u2014 and it is at \u039b\u2089\u2032, the only constraint graph in the tower carrying a cycle. The law is a theorem about trees and fails at exactly the stage that stopped being one. A prior version ('opposition fails at two-parent coordinates') is withdrawn: at \u039b\u2088 g has two parents and no child, so the cause is childlessness, not parentage."}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_two_parent_coordinate_g", "label": "g, the Unique Two-Parent Bound in the Tower", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every coordinate from the ninth axis to the thirteenth enters with exactly one parent, which is why closure survives thirteen dimensions and forty-seven million ambient cells; the two places a second could have entered are the two places the book records a price (\u039b\u2089\u2032 and \u039b\u2081\u2082's K)."}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_second_bridge_census", "label": "Every Second Bridge at the Top of the Tower", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Fifty-eight of sixty-four second bridges destroy the \u039b\u2081\u2083 factorisation (defects 1,794 to 82,680); the six that do not are the six that reduce the object to a remnant. q is the unique cut vertex separating the two ends, so the forbidden bridge does not add a new connection \u2014 it adds a second one, which is what a tree forbids."}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_tight_k_discrepancy", "label": "The Tight K and a Discrepancy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The rebuild reproduces all seven tower cell counts, the four-cap sweep, the 41,682 composition pairs and \u00a712.11.5's four sections exactly, and gives the true breakage fraction as 21.4 % at \u039b\u2081\u2082 and 22.8 % at \u039b\u2081\u2083 \u2014 not constant, rising to 35.3 % at f_max = 2. The price of keeping the tree grows with the shell the index carries."}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_no_doubly_irreducible_cell", "label": "No Cell Is Doubly Irreducible", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Recomputed at cap 20 the E1 puncture shows 0 join failures and 4 meet failures, all four producing (0,0). Four is near the floor: the forbidden cell is among the least-defended its index has, and the index still refuses to lose it."}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_reversal", "label": "The Reversal (rev(\u039b\u2089), 1,654 cells, closed)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_groupoid_intersection", "label": "The Intersection Is a Groupoid (389 cells, 4,887 composable pairs)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_newparts_union_does_not_exist", "label": "The Union Does Not Exist (E = 2,857)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_newparts_parts_v_to_viii", "target": "recovered_newparts_balance_defect_1268", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_newparts_parts_v_to_viii", "target": "recovered_newparts_pushback", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_newparts_parts_v_to_viii", "target": "recovered_newparts_cut_law", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_newparts_pushback", "target": "recovered_newparts_step_law", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_newparts_pushback", "target": "recovered_newparts_no_doubly_irreducible_cell", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_newparts_cut_law", "target": "recovered_newparts_two_parent_coordinate_g", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_newparts_two_parent_coordinate_g", "target": "recovered_newparts_second_bridge_census", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "recovered/newparts.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "recovered_newparts_second_bridge_census", "target": "recovered_newparts_tight_k_discrepancy", "relation": "references", 